This folder contains the code to generate sum-of-exponents approximation tables for Caputo fractional derivative.
Generated tables can be used with fractional derivative nonlinear viscoelastic model, located in examples/tutorials/nonlin_viscoelast_incompress.cpp

In order to run Python code using Linux/Ubuntu machine, you can use the following steps
(steps below are run from this directory):

- Prepare virtual environment for locally installed packages and activate it:
	mkdir venv
	python -m venv venv
	source venv/bin/activate
- Install required packages:
	pip install -r requirements.txt
- Run code in virtual environment (see source to override default parameters to adapt it for your case):
	python baryrat_generate.py

Code generates table for the order of Caputo fractional derivative alpha = [0.01 0.02 .. 0.99]

